      ],
      "content": "exact meaning unknown. MED defines knoppe as an ornamental knob (MED s.v. knop(pe n. (1)), but does not attest, much less define key knoppe. The Cologne translations are ‘a hook for keys’ (schlüssel hacken) and ‘a knob for keys’ (schlüssel knoüff), but that is also unattested | exact meaning unknown. MED defines knoppe as an ornamental knob (MED s.v. knop(pe n. (1)), but does not attest, much less define key knob. The Cologne translations of the Books of Rates describe this as ‘a hook for keys’ (schlüssel hacken) and ‘a knob for keys’ (schlüssel knoüff), but that is also unattested (Jenks 2024, p. 283)) | key knopp(e), a term whose exact meaning is unknown. MED defines knoppe as an ornamental knob (MED s.v. knop(pe n. (1)), but does not attest, much less define key knoppe. The Cologne translations (in the Book of Rates) are ‘a hook for keys’ (schlüssel hacken) and ‘a knob for keys’ (schlüssel knoüff), but that is also unattested)"
    }
